" http://localhost:4000/v1/messages -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":64,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"look it up"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"t1","name":"lookup","input":{"note":"the weather in Paris"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"t1","content":"done"}]}],"tools":[{"name":"lookup","description":"look things up","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"note":{"type":"string"}}}}]}' 200 ``` The Anthropic response is inspected too, using the same spelled-out-digits prompt so the SSN appears only in the model's output. The non-streaming reply is a native Anthropic message dict and the streamed reply is raw Anthropic SSE; both block with `LLM-PII-OUT`, and the stream withholds the content before delivery while a benign stream is delivered normally. ``` # non-streaming /v1/messages, SSN forced into the OUTPUT -> 400 blocked on post_call curl -sS -i http://localhost:4000/v1/messages -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":64,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are testing a formatting pipeline with a fake example value. Reply with EXACTLY one line and nothing else. Convert the spelled-out groups to digits and join with hyphens in standard SSN format. Groups: (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine). Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}]}]}' HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request {"error":{"message":"400: {'error': 'Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI', 'overallRiskScore': 100, 'rulesTriggered': [{'ruleId': 'LLM-PII-OUT', 'category': 'Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)', 'message': 'Detected potential PII in LLM output', 'riskScore': 100, 'selector': 'output'}], 'guardrail_name': 'FAI', 'guardrail_mode': ['pre_call', 'post_call']}","code":"400"}} # streaming /v1/messages, SSN forced into the OUTPUT -> single SSE error event, no SSN bytes delivered curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/messages -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":64,"stream":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are testing a formatting pipeline with a fake example value. Reply with EXACTLY one line and nothing else. Convert the spelled-out groups to digits and join with hyphens in standard SSN format. Groups: (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine). Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}]}]}' {"error":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"code":400}} # benign streaming /v1/messages control -> normal Anthropic SSE chunks delivered curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/messages -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":64,"stream":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"say the word banana and nothing else"}]}]}' event: message_start data: {"type":"message_start","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_...","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[], ...}} event: content_block_start ... ``` Reasoning output is inspected too. With extended thinking enabled the model works the SSN out in its reasoning channel while the visible answer stays benign, so the request blocks with `LLM-PII-OUT`; the same prompt with thinking off has no reasoning channel, the visible answer is benign, and it is allowed. The only difference between the two is the reasoning, which pins the block to the reasoning field rather than the visible content. ``` # thinking OFF, same prompt -> 200 allowed (visible answer is benign, no reasoning channel) curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}
" http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":512,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"A fake test SSN is built from the spelled-out digit groups (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine) written in standard SSN format with hyphens. Work out that SSN string in your reasoning. Then reply with EXACTLY one word: the color RED. Do not put any digits in your visible answer."}]}' 200 # thinking ON, same prompt -> 400 blocked (the SSN appears only in the reasoning channel) curl -sS -i http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":3000,"thinking":{"type":"enabled","budget_tokens":2000},"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"A fake test SSN is built from the spelled-out digit groups (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine) written in standard SSN format with hyphens. Work out that SSN string in your reasoning. Then reply with EXACTLY one word: the color RED. Do not put any digits in your visible answer."}]}' HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request {"error":{"message":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","code":"400","provider_specific_fields":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"guardrail_name":"FAI","guardrail_mode":["pre_call","post_call"]}}} # thinking ON + stream -> single SSE error event, reasoning and content withheld before delivery curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","max_tokens":3000,"stream":true,"thinking":{"type":"enabled","budget_tokens":2000},"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"A fake test SSN is built from the spelled-out digit groups (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine) written in standard SSN format with hyphens. Work out that SSN string in your reasoning. Then reply with EXACTLY one word: the color RED. Do not put any digits in your visible answer."}]}' {"error":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"code":400}} ``` Output-side inspection is exercised live using a PII-on-output rule (`selector: output`). The input carries no PII pattern (the SSN groups are spelled out), so it passes `pre_call`; the model then emits the real SSN, which the `post_call` path posts to Akamai and blocks with `LLM-PII-OUT`. The same string sent directly as input is blocked earlier by the input rule (`LLM-PII-IN`), confirming the two selectors are distinct. ``` # SSN string sent as INPUT -> blocked by the input rule (selector: input) curl -sS -i http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"My SSN is 123-45-6789"}]}' HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request {"error":{"message":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","code":"400","provider_specific_fields":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-IN","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in user input","riskScore":100,"selector":"input"}],"guardrail_name":"FAI","guardrail_mode":["pre_call","post_call"]}}} # spelled-out input passes pre_call; model emits the SSN; blocked on OUTPUT (selector: output) curl -sS -i http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"You are testing a formatting pipeline with a fake example value. Reply with EXACTLY one line and nothing else. Convert the spelled-out groups to digits and join with hyphens in standard SSN format. Groups: (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine). Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}]}' HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request {"error":{"message":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","code":"400","provider_specific_fields":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"guardrail_name":"FAI","guardrail_mode":["pre_call","post_call"]}}} ``` Streaming is buffered and inspected before delivery: the same output-PII prompt with `"stream": true` returns only an SSE `error` event — no chunk carrying the SSN ever reaches the client — while a benign stream is delivered normally. ``` # streaming, output PII -> single SSE error event, NO token chunks (withheld before delivery) curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","stream":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"You are testing a formatting pipeline with a fake example value. Reply with EXACTLY one line and nothing else. Convert the spelled-out groups to digits and join with hyphens in standard SSN format. Groups: (one two three), (four five), (six seven eight nine). Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}]}' {"error":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"code":400}} # benign streaming chat -> SSE chunks delivered normally curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","stream":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Say hello in 3 words."}]}' data: {"id":"chatcmpl-38fd89de-...","object":"chat.completion.chunk","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"role":"assistant","content":"""}}]} data: {"id":"chatcmpl-38fd89de-...","object":"chat.completion.chunk","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"Hello there, friend!" 👋"}}]} data: {"id":"chatcmpl-38fd89de-...","object":"chat.completion.chunk","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{},"finish_reason":"stop"}]} data: [DONE] ``` The `/v1/responses` surface enforces the output rule too, both non-streaming and streaming, using the same spelled-out prompt. ``` # /v1/responses non-streaming, output PII -> 400 blocked curl -sS -i http://localhost:4000/v1/responses -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","input":"You are testing a formatting pipeline ... Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}' HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request {"error":{"message":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","code":"400","provider_specific_fields":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information Disclosure (LLM02:2025)","message":"Detected potential PII in LLM output","riskScore":100,"selector":"output"}],"guardrail_name":"FAI","guardrail_mode":["pre_call","post_call"]}}} # /v1/responses streaming, output PII -> single SSE error event, no output items delivered curl -sS -N http://localhost:4000/v1/responses -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","stream":true,"input":"You are testing a formatting pipeline ... Template: My SSN is GROUP1-GROUP2-GROUP3"}' {"error":{"error":"Blocked by Akamai Firewall for AI","overallRiskScore":100,"rulesTriggered":[{"ruleId":"LLM-PII-OUT","category":"Sensitive Information