## TLDR Problem this solves: - The strict tag-denial pin asserted only "a 401 came back" - Any unrelated 401, like a dead key, kept it green - The e2e harness threw 401 bodies away, so no pin could check the cause How it solves it: - `UnauthorizedError` now carries the 401 body, as `RateLimitedError` already does for 429s - The pin asserts the tag-routing denial message, not just the status - Proven by mutation: the same wrong-cause 401 passes before, fails after ## User Flow Before: a platform admin's tag fence quietly stops being enforced, and the release gate meant to guard it waves the change through 1. The admin registers a deployment under the name `tier-b-only` with POST https://litellm-domain/model/new 2. They mint a key scoped to that deployment with POST https://litellm-domain/key/generate carrying `"router_settings": {"enable_tag_filtering": true}` 3. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "tier-b-only"` and `"tags": ["tier-b"]`, and get 401 `Not allowed to access model due to tags configuration. Passed model=tier-b-only and tags=['tier-b']`, which is the fence doing its job 4. A later release changes what that same request does: it still comes back 401, but the message now reads `Authentication Error, Invalid proxy server token passed`, so the tag fence is no longer what refused it 5. The release gate stays green through all of it, because it only ever reads the 401 status and never the reason 6. Consequence: a teammate whose key is not entitled to a tagged tier can start reaching it, and nothing in the release process catches the regression that let them in After: the same drift turns the release gate red on the reason, not just the status, so the fence is verified before anyone ships 1. The admin registers a deployment under the name `tier-b-only` with POST https://litellm-domain/model/new 2. They mint a key scoped to that deployment with POST https://litellm-domain/key/generate carrying `"router_settings": {"enable_tag_filtering": true}` 3. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "tier-b-only"` and `"tags": ["tier-b"]`, and get 401 `Not allowed to access model due to tags configuration. Passed model=tier-b-only and tags=['tier-b']`, which is the fence doing its job 4. A later release changes what that same request does: it still comes back 401, but the message now reads `Authentication Error, Invalid proxy server token passed`, so the tag fence is no longer what refused it 5. The release gate turns red on that release and names the reason: `expected the denial to come from tag routing, got a 401 reading {"error":{"message":"Authentication Error, Invalid proxy server token passed..."` 6. Consequence: the same teammate stays fenced out of the tagged tier, because a release that stops enforcing tags can no longer pass the gate ## Relevant issues Follows up on #37366, which added the pin ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5792 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Shared setup, a live proxy on localhost:44878 with `store_model_in_db: true`, showing that the proxy hands back two 401s the old pin could not tell apart: ```bash curl -s -X POST http://localhost:44878/model/new -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"model_name":"qa-untagged-tier","litellm_params":{"model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5"}}' KEY=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:44878/key/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-1234" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"models":["qa-untagged-tier"],"router_settings":{"enable_tag_filtering":true}}' | jq -r .key) # A: the denial the pin is supposed to be watching curl -s -w "
