p %N' $HOME/.litellm $HOME/.litellm/token.json`, and the keychain stays empty ``` drwx------ .../fakehome_headless/.litellm -rw------- .../fakehome_headless/.litellm/token.json $ security find-generic-password -s litellm-cli -a credential security: SecKeychainSearchCopyNext: The specified item could not be found in the keychain. ``` 3. A real completion still succeeds on that fallback credential ```json { "id": "chatcmpl-b692b572-110f-4e69-9e7c-4c10b4a71fb3", "model": "haiku", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": { "content": "AFTER LEG headless file fallback credential authenticated this call.", "role": "assistant"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 17, "prompt_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 47} } ``` #### A credential from an older `lite` The fixture is a `token.json` in exactly the shape the merge base writes, carrying a live credential, 0600 inside a 0755 `~/.litellm`, with the keychain empty. 1. It authenticates with no prompt to sign in again ```json { "id": "chatcmpl-ff880593-a396-4485-ad59-02bd0fd4635d", "model": "haiku", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": { "content": "AFTER LEG legacy token migrated without re-login.", "role": "assistant"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 16, "prompt_tokens": 29, "total_tokens": 45} } ``` 2. The keychain now holds it: `security find-generic-password -s litellm-cli -a credential` ``` keychain: "/Users/mateo/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db" class: "genp" attributes: 0x00000007 <blob>="litellm-cli" "acct"<blob>="credential" "cdat"<timedate>=0x32303236303832303032323532305A00 "20260820022520Z\000" ``` 3. The file no longer carries it, and the directory got tightened on the way ``` $ cat $HOME/.litellm/token.json { "base_url": "http://localhost:8462", "user_id": "cli-repro-admin", "user_email": "unknown", "user_role": "cli", "auth_header_name": "Authorization", "jwt_token": "", "timestamp": 1787192623.0960488 } $ stat -f '%Sp %N' $HOME/.litellm $HOME/.litellm/token.json drwx------ .../fakehome_legacy/.litellm -rw------- .../fakehome_legacy/.litellm/token.json ``` #### Logout 1. `lite --base-url http://localhost:8462 logout` ``` Logged out successfully. Authentication token cleared. ``` 2. Both stores are clear, and the CLI knows it ``` $ ls -la $HOME/.litellm total 0 drwx------@ 2 mateo staff 64 Aug 19 19:23 . $ security find-generic-password -s litellm-cli -a credential security: SecKeychainSearchCopyNext: The specified item could not be found in the keychain. $ lite --base-url http://localhost:8462 whoami Not authenticated. Run 'lite login' to authenticate. ``` #### Flag and env precedence 1. `--api-key` still outranks the stored credential: `lite --base-url http://localhost:8462 --api-key sk-wrong-key-after-leg http request POST /v1/chat/completions -j '{...}'` ``` Error: HTTP 401 {"error": {"message": "Authentication Error, Invalid proxy server token passed. Received API Key = sk-...-leg, ... Unable to find token in cache or `LiteLLM_VerificationTokenTable`", "type": "token_not_found_in_db", "param": "key", "code": "401"}} ``` 2. `LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY` still outranks it too ``` Error: HTTP 401 {"error": {"message": "Authentication Error, Invalid proxy server token passed. Received API Key = sk-...-leg, ... Unable to find token in cache or `LiteLLM_VerificationTokenTable`", "type": "token_not_found_in_db", "param": "key", "code": "401"}} ``` 3. With neither set, the stored credential works again ```json { "id": "chatcmpl-6e22983f-930e-4288-949a-1d2ddcb4dcf1", "model": "haiku", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": { "content": "AFTER LEG stored credential still wins when no flag or env var is set.", "role": "assistant"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 20, "prompt_tokens": 33, "total_tokens": 53} } ``` ### What the run turned up alongside the result - Only the directory was 0755; the file was already 0600 - So other accounts could traverse, not read the file - Same-user processes were the real exposure, and still are - Redirecting `$HOME` alone makes the macOS keychain unreachable - That path falls back to the file, correctly and loudly - Legacy migration also tightens an existing 0755 directory - Keychain blob pairs base_url with key, blocking cross-server reuse - An empty bearer answers "Malformed API Key", not "no key" - `lite whoami` exits 0 even when not authenticated - SSO returned proxy_admin, but token.json records `user_role: cli` - Those last three predate this PR and are untouched by it ## Type 🆕 New Feature ## Caveats (if any) - Revoking a live CLI session ships separately in #36846 - `keyring` installs with the `cli` extra - Headless boxes keep today's file-based exposure ### Final Attestation - [ ] The tests check the right things, including the edge cases, and regressions in the respective real-world customer use-cases are not possible after this PR

