## TLDR Problem this solves: - Gemini 3 Flash and 3.1 Pro Preview require 4,096 tokens for explicit caching - LiteLLM's cost map lacked `prompt_cache_min_tokens`, so the 1,024 default applied - Caches between 1,024 and 4,095 tokens hit Vertex's hard 400 How it solves it: - Sets `prompt_cache_min_tokens: 4096` on all 15 affected entries in both maps - LiteLLM now skips explicit cache creation below Google's documented minimum ## User Flow Before: a developer sending Vertex Gemini 3 Flash requests with a `cache_control` prompt prefix between 1,024 and 4,095 tokens gets a hard 400 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "gemini-3.5-flash"` and a ~2,800-token system message marked `"cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}` 2. The response is HTTP 400: `litellm.BadRequestError: Vertex_aiException BadRequestError - "The cached content is of 2791 tokens. The minimum token count to start explicit caching is 4096."` 3. The same request on gemini-3.6-flash and gemini-3.7-flash fails with the same 400, and the same prompt sent through POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses fails identically After: the same request returns a normal completion 1. They send the same POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with the same `cache_control` system message 2. The response is HTTP 200 with the model's answer; no cache-creation call is attempted below 4,096 tokens 3. The same prompt through POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses also returns HTTP 200 4. Prefixes of 4,096 tokens and above still create the explicit cache and get the cached-token discount ## Relevant issues `prompt_cache_min_tokens` was introduced in #33637. This carries the diff from #37427 (closed) onto an internal branch and completes it with the three `gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools` entries its review flagged as missing ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5793 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I