## TLDR Problem this solves: - Freeform (custom) tool calls log no output to Langfuse - Every code-mode turn looks like the model answered nothing How it solves it: - Map `custom_tool_call` output items into the Langfuse output payload ## User Flow Before: a developer proxying a coding agent that uses a freeform `exec` tool sees blank outputs in Langfuse, so a whole session reads as if the model never answered 1. They send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses` with `"tools": [{"type": "custom", "name": "exec", ...}]` 2. The response comes back with a `custom_tool_call` item carrying the JavaScript to run, and the agent runs it 3. They open that generation in Langfuse: **Output is `null`**, while input, token counts and cost are all correct 4. Every turn where the model called `exec` looks empty, so the trace can't be used to review what the agent actually did After: the same request records the tool call it actually made 1. They send the same `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses` with the same custom tool 2. The response comes back with the same `custom_tool_call` item, and the agent runs it 3. They open that generation in Langfuse: **Output shows the call** — `[{"id": "...", "name": "exec", "call_id": "call_...", "type": "custom_tool_call", "input": "console.log(6*7)
"}]` 4. Turns that called `exec` are reviewable alongside the plain-text and `function_call` turns that already worked ## Relevant issues Fixes #37430 ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [ ] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) — `lint` is green; the only red check is `misc / Run tests`, failing on `tests/test_litellm/batches/test_batch_utils.py::test_handle_completed_vertex_batch_computes_cost_usage_and_models` (a Vertex batch cost assertion), which is red on other open PRs against the same base and is unrelated to this change - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Real `/v1/responses` calls through a proxy I ran locally, against a live `gpt-5.6-sol` deployment, exporting to a self-hosted Langfuse. No mocks. Same request both times; only the checked-out revision of `langfuse_otel.py` differs. Shared setup — `config.yaml`: ```yaml model_list: - model_name: gpt-5.6-sol litellm_params: model: openai/gpt-5.6-sol api_base: http://<upstream-gateway>/v1 api_key: <redacted> model_info: mode: responses litellm_settings: callbacks: ["langfuse_otel"] ``` Env: `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` / `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` (redacted), `LANGFUSE_HOST=https://<self-hosted-langfuse>`. Request used in both runs: ```json {"model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "input": "Use the exec tool to print 6*7 in JavaScript.", "tools": [{"type": "custom", "name": "exec", "description": "Run JavaScript and return stdout"}], "tool_choice": "required", "store": false} ``` ### Before (`423b791`, this PR's merge base) 1. Send the request: ```console $ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:47311/v1/responses -H "authorization: Bearer $KEY" \ -H 'content-type: application/json' --data-binary @probe.json -w 'http=%{http_code}
